    "summary": "Added the C++ reader (src/indexer/parser/cpp.ts) for .cpp/.cc/.cxx/.hpp/.hh/.hxx/.h, behind the guarded load. It reads classes and structs with INHERITS from their bases, and members as Class::name with their access. Qualified out-of-line definitions are attached to their class. Free functions and prototypes are kept (a definition takes precedence), and types are read. Namespaces are folded into names; a function in an anonymous namespace or declared static is not exported. Includes and calls are handled as in C. Left out: calls through an object (obj.m()) are not recorded, and an unqualified name inside a namespace matches only a target of exactly that name.",
